also_stated_at:
Roughly, a second-order $(\varepsilon, \theta)$-approximate local minimum of a function $\psi: \mathbb{R}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is a point $x^\star$ which satisfies the following second-order conditions

$$\|\nabla \psi(x^\star)\| \leq \varepsilon \ \  \mbox{and} 
 \ \ \lambda_{\mathrm{min}}( \nabla^2 \psi(x^\star)) \geq -\theta.$$

